To add a link to each post, you'll need to modify your Nginx configuration to include a link in your HTML pages. Specifically, you'll need to add a link tag in your `index.html` file and update your `location /` block to serve the `index.html` file.

Here's an updated configuration that adds a link to each post:
```nginx
server {
    listen 443 ssl http2;
    listen [::]:443 ssl http2;
    server_name www.askfundu.com;
    root /usr/share/nginx/html;

    # SSL
    ssl_certificate /etc/nginx/server.crt;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/private.key;

    # logging
    access_log /var/log/nginx/access.log combined buffer=512k flush=1m;
    error_log /var/log/nginx/error.log warn;

    # index.html fallback
    location / {
        root /usr/share/nginx/html;
        index index.html index.htm;
        try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;

        # Add a link to each post
        add_header Link "<https://www.askfundu.com/post/%{uri}>;rel=prev";

        # Match each post and add a link
        if ($uri ~* "^/post/) {
            set $link "<https://www.askfundu.com/post/%{uri}>";
            add_header Link $link;역8820.000000/

        }
    }

    error_page 500 502 503 504 /50x.html;

    location = /50x.html {
        root /usr/share/nginx/html;
    }

    # Backend Configuration (Added for testing)
    #location /api {
    #    proxy_pass https://askfundu.com:5000;
    #    proxy_set_header Host $host;
    #    proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
    #    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    #}
}
```
In the above configuration, I added the following:

1. `add_header Link "<https://www.askfundu.com/post/%{uri}>;rel=prev"`: This adds a link header to the `index.html` file, which will be inherited by all HTML pages served by Nginx. The link will point to the current URL with the `post/` prefix.
2. `if ($uri ~* "^/post/") { ... }`: This block matches each post URL and sets a variable called `$link` to the URL of the current post. The `add_header` directive is then used to add the link header to the response.
3. `set $link "<https://www.askfundu.com/post/%{uri}>";`: This sets the `$link` variable to the URL of the current post.

Now, when you access any URL on your website, Nginx will add a link header to the response. You can then access this link in your HTML pages using JavaScript or CSS.

For example, in your `index.html` file, you can add the following code to display the link:
```html
<link rel="prev" href="{{ Link }}"> Previous Post
